  "description": "A byte-identical redelivery of an already-accepted message is ALREADY_RECORDED and performs no writes.",
  "why_it_exists": "Inbound delivery is at-least-once. Without a stored ingress fingerprint a redelivered message either appended a duplicate inbound row and a duplicate action, or - once a wall-clock value entered the fingerprint - a plain retry looked like a tampered message and raised a false IDEMPOTENCY_CONFLICT. The fingerprint is now derived only from the raw message, and every replay outcome is decided before the classifier runs. Covers suite cases R1-R6 and E1.",
